    body: 'Medical coding is desk-based, detail-heavy, and repetitive by design: reading physician notes, matching them to precise codes, hitting accuracy and productivity targets every day. If you get restless doing the same category of task for hours, plan an early move into auditing, training, or client-facing coordination rather than staying a production coder for a decade.',
    note: 'The job rewards patience and precision far more than it rewards multitasking energy.',
